turn docs (often redundant with prose; use when type\u002Fbehavior isn't obvious).",[177,312,313,318],{},[223,314,315],{},[18,316,317],{},"# Notes"," — extra info that doesn't fit elsewhere.",[14,320,321],{},"The order convention (Examples, Panics, Errors, Safety) puts the most useful (examples) first and the most critical (safety contracts) prominently.",[323,324,325,338],"table",{},[326,327,328],"thead",{},[329,330,331,335],"tr",{},[332,333,334],"th",{},"Section",[332,336,337],{},"Purpose",[339,340,341,351,360,374,385,394,403],"tbody",{},[329,342,343,348],{},[344,345,346],"td",{},[18,347,235],{},[344,349,350],{},"Usage examples (run as doc tests).",[329,352,353,357],{},[344,354,355],{},[18,356,243],{},[344,358,359],{},"When the function panics.",[329,361,362,366],{},[344,363,364],{},[18,365,268],{},[344,367,368,369,272,371,373],{},"For ",[18,370,250],{},[18,372,275],{}," variants.",[329,375,376,380],{},[344,377,378],{},[18,379,283],{},[344,381,368,382,384],{},[18,383,286],{}," functions: required invariants.",[329,386,387,391],{},[344,388,389],{},[18,390,305],{},[344,392,393],{},"Parameter docs (sometimes redundant with prose).",[329,395,396,400],{},[344,397,398],{},[18,399,309],{},[344,401,402],{},"Return value docs.",[329,404,405,409],{},[344,406,407],{},[18,408,317],{},[344,410,411],{},"Extra info.",[14,413,414],{},"The order convention: Examples, Panics, Errors, Safety.",[27,416,418],{"id":417},"cross-references","Cross-References",[32,420,421],{"language":34},[36,422,424],{"className":38,"code":423,"language":34,"meta":40,"style":40},"\u002F\u002F\u002F See [`std::fs::read`] for reading a file.\n\u002F\u002F\u002F Uses [`OtherType::method`] internally.\n\u002F\u002F\u002F Implements [`MyTrait`].\n",[18,425,426,431,436],{"__ignoreMap":40},[44,427,428],{"class":46,"line":47},[44,429,430],{"class":50},"\u002F\u002F\u002F See [`std::fs::read`] for reading a file.\n",[44,432,433],{"class":46,"line":54},[44,434,435],{"class":50},"\u002F\u002F\u002F Uses [`OtherType