ture only\" banner\n",[27,719,721],{"id":720},"lints","Lints",[215,723,725],{"id":724},"why-these-matter-and-when-to-enable","Why these matter and when to enable",[14,727,728,729,145],{},"Doc lints enforce ",[223,730,731],{},"documentation as a gate, not a reminder",[174,733,734,762,777,785],{},[177,735,736,741,742,745,746,749,750,753,754,757,758,761],{},[223,737,738],{},[18,739,740],{},"missing_docs"," — every public item must have docs; turns \"forgot to document\" into a build error. Reach for it in ",[223,743,744],{},"libraries"," where the public API ",[258,747,748],{},"is"," the product — it prevents silently shipping undocumented items. Enable in ",[18,751,752],{},"lib.rs"," with ",[18,755,756],{},"#![warn(missing_docs)]"," (or ",[18,759,760],{},"deny"," for strict libraries).",[177,763,764,769,770,773,774,776],{},[223,765,766],{},[18,767,768],{},"missing_debug_implementations"," — every public type must impl ",[18,771,772],{},"Debug"," (derive or manual). ",[18,775,772],{}," is essential for diagnostics; this lint catches types you forgot to derive it on.",[177,778,779,784],{},[223,780,781],{},[18,782,783],{},"rustdoc::broken_intra_doc_links"," — intra-doc links that don't resolve (a renamed item, a typo) become errors. Reach for it so stale links surface immediately, not after a docs.rs build.",[177,786,787,792,793,795],{},[223,788,789],{},[18,790,791],{},"rustdoc::missing_crate_level_docs"," — requires the ",[18,794,186],{}," crate-level doc comment (the landing page). Reach for it so every crate has an intro.",[14,797,798,799,802,803,806,807,809],{},"Enable these as a library matures — early prototypes can ",[18,800,801],{},"allow",", but a published library should ",[18,804,805],{},"warn","\u002F",[18,808,760],{}," them so the docs stay complete and correct.",[32,811,812],{"language":34},[36,813,815],{"className":38,"code":814,"language":34,"meta":40,"style":40},"#![warn(missing_docs)]\n#![warn(missing_debug_implementations)]\n#![warn(rustdoc::broken_int